BT /F1 11 Tf 48 736 Td 24 TL (Sample science notes: Electricity) Tj T* (Original practice material for testing NCERT Tutor, not an official textbook.) Tj T* (Electric current is the rate of flow of electric charge. I = Q / t.) Tj T* (The SI unit of current is the ampere. An ammeter is connected in series.) Tj T* (Potential difference is work done per unit charge. V = W / Q.) Tj T* (The SI unit of potential difference is the volt.) Tj T* (Ohm's law: at constant temperature, voltage equals current times resistance.) Tj T* (V = I R. Resistance is measured in ohms.) Tj T* (Example: 6 volts across 3 ohms produces a current of 2 amperes.) Tj ET
