BT /F1 11 Tf 48 736 Td 24 TL (Sample science notes: Circuits and power) Tj T* (In a series circuit, the same current flows through every resistor.) Tj T* (Total series resistance is R = R1 + R2 + R3.) Tj T* (In a parallel circuit, each branch has the same potential difference.) Tj T* (For parallel resistors, 1/R = 1/R1 + 1/R2 + 1/R3.) Tj T* (Electric power is the rate of transfer of electrical energy.) Tj T* (P = V I. Using Ohm's law, P = I squared R, and P = V squared / R.) Tj T* (The SI unit of power is the watt. Energy transferred is E = P t.) Tj T* (Example: a 60 watt lamp used for 2 hours consumes 120 watt-hours.) Tj T* (A fuse protects a circuit by melting when the current is too large.) Tj ET
